{"result":{"finish_reason":"eos","image_tokens":483,"precision":"int8_weights_dynamic_activations","text":"<|det|>title [27, 64, 316, 104]<|/det|>WATER QUALITY FIELD REPORT\n<|det|>text [27, 118, 636, 163]<|/det|>Station: Willow Creek East Survey: WC-1186 Date: 28 September 2026\n<|det|>text [27, 228, 636, 272]<|/det|>The morning survey covered the upstream bridge and the southern footpath.\n<|det|>text [27, 282, 607, 325]<|/det|>Three sealed samples were collected before the first scheduled discharge.\n<|det|>text [27, 338, 588, 382]<|/det|>Sample A: 08:15, temperature 18.4 C, pH 7.2, conductivity 412 uS/cm.\n<|det|>text [27, 392, 591, 435]<|/det|>Sample B: 08:27, temperature 18.6 C, pH 7.1, conductivity 409 uS/cm.\n<|det|>text [27, 447, 591, 491]<|/det|>Sample C: 08:42, temperature 18.5 C, pH 7.3, conductivity 415 uS/cm.\n<|det|>text [27, 554, 654, 598]<|/det|>No visible surface film was observed. The water appeared clear at all locations.\n<|det|>text [27, 609, 675, 653]<|/det|>Each sample bottle was labelled, photographed, and placed in the transport case.\n<|det|>text [27, 664, 664, 707]<|/det|>Laboratory results are pending; these observations are not a safety certification.\n<|det|>text [27, 774, 562, 818]<|/det|>Prepared by: Field Operations Reviewed by: Laboratory Services","timings":{"decode_seconds":2.238100584999999,"decode_steps":355,"first_token_seconds":3.187873166,"prefill_seconds":0.675441917,"preprocess_seconds":0.019761166,"total_seconds":5.455670333,"vision_seconds":2.492583417},"token_ids":[128818,10212,764,1477,14,223,2892,14,223,17998,14,223,7163,63,128819,57,55697,107150,14167,103095,77929,201,128818,2067,764,1477,14,223,8610,14,223,26500,14,223,9265,63,128819,48846,28,88754,23859,7726,19592,28,51584,15,8610,24,7222,28,223,1449,5773,223,939,24,201,128818,2067,764,1477,14,223,15539,14,223,26500,14,223,16879,63,128819,671,7469,9272,10077,270,43661,15986,305,270,16003,5539,9860,603,128818,2067,764,1477,14,223,17961,14,223,26105,14,223,17332,63,1